Z||000000||Xtreme Fiero's||11-09-2000||08:14 PM||||<BR>I have just seen a new Water:Air intercooler from JR it looks like the Intercooler is fitted to the intake piping from there supercahrger to the Throttle body (miata not honda) it is abou 10"long and 5" round. A water pump circulates the coolant to a heat exchanger mounted in the nose of the car.<BR>    if the Heat exchanger is not to big maybe it could be mounted in the rear right fenderwell or if the pump could take it even in the nose of our cars.<BR>    SCC's test #'s say the JR supercharged & intercooled '99 Miata made 51.2 more HP and 40.3 HP at 7PSI||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||11-10-2000||08:14 AM||||NO.. it needs direct air flow to work properly! the air/liquid is WAY more efficent than Air/Air you can install and additional cooling can for SUPER cooling the glycal with dry ice or water ice mix. but the heat exchanger need LOTS of air...<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 11-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Xtreme Fiero's||11-10-2000||08:59 AM||||But it's not Air:Air it's Water:Air is it still the same deal? What if a bigget watter pump was added? then it could be run in the front behind a Areo nose.||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||11-10-2000||09:08 AM||||there is a air/liquid heat exchanger that extracts the heat from the charge air heated intercooler core liquid. you'll have to run plumbing from the intercooler to the front of the car for the heat exchanger then back to a super cooler catch can then into the air/liquid intercooler at the intake. the pump provided will do just fine... but make sure the intercooler heat exchanger is in from of ALL your other radiator stuff... A/C core, and radiator and any trans cooler you might have. don't put it in the fender well you'll and don't try and force air into the engine bay from the top of the car. <A HREF="http://www.f-max.com" TARGET=_blank>www.f-max.com</A>  for water injection for even more detonation control!<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/chart_.jpg">   <P><BR>well what says exhaust should say heated charge air<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 11-10-2000).]||||reg||1
